Subject: Competitive play: a set's cheats
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

RANKED plays without the game's cheats: GameInfoManager asks for them only in
offline friendly matches and online ones off the ranked ladder (UseAltRules).
A set's rules may pick a stadium, player and power-up cheat, the same for both
games. While a match plays by a set's rules (mscharged_competitive_cheats,
src/platform/competitive_match.cpp), GetActiveRules returns the set's cheats
and every cheat check reads them; anything else is unchanged.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_competitive.h b/include/mscharged_competitive.h
--- a/include/mscharged_competitive.h
+++ b/include/mscharged_competitive.h
@@ -94,6 +94,14 @@
 bool mscharged_competitive_fit_text(void* text, void* matrix);
 #endif
 
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+// A set's cheats (tweak patch 0060): true while this match plays by a set's
+// rules, with its stadium cheat (eEnvironmentCheat), player cheat
+// (ePlayerCheat) and power-up cheat (ePowerupCheat) in the non-null
+// pointers. Both games play by them; RANKED otherwise has none.
+bool mscharged_competitive_cheats(int* stadium, int* player, int* powerup);
+#endif
+
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
 #endif
